WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.750 --> 00:00:19.115
closed for winter vacation, and when it reopened in February, Davy and Dora were new students in first

2
00:00:19.175 --> 00:00:25.620
grade. "I think school is great fun," Davy told Marilla after his first day at school.

3
00:00:26.656 --> 00:00:30.998
"You said I'd find it hard to sit still, and I did but I can wriggle my legs

4
00:00:31.058 --> 00:00:32.499
under the desk, and that helps.

5
00:00:34.059 --> 00:00:40.102
Christopher Cotton drew a picture of Anne on his slate," Davy continued, "and it was really ugly, so

6
00:00:40.142 --> 00:00:41.863
I told him I'd hit him at recess.

7
00:00:42.563 --> 00:00:48.085
Christopher said he wasn't scared of me, but he rubbed out Anne's name and put Barbara Shaw's instead."

8
00:00:49.106 --> 00:00:49.966
Marilla frowned.

9
00:00:50.546 --> 00:00:53.567
She wasn't pleased that Davy was making threats at school.

10
00:00:53.587 --> 00:00:58.467
"Well, at least he is making friends," she thought a moment later.

11
00:01:00.069 --> 00:01:03.572
One Friday afternoon Diana and Anne met at Green Gables.

12
00:01:05.413 --> 00:01:10.338
They had been invited to tea at Diana's cousin's house in Grafton and had decided to walk.

13
00:01:11.479 --> 00:01:15.542
When they came to a fork in the road, they took the left road when they should have

14
00:01:15.582 --> 00:01:16.303
taken the right.

15
00:01:17.464 --> 00:01:18.585
Soon they were lost.

16
00:01:18.605 --> 00:01:20.346
"Where are we?"

17
00:01:20.787 --> 00:01:21.728
exclaimed Diana.

18
00:01:23.800 --> 00:01:26.741
"Oh, we must have taken a wrong turn," said Anne.

19
00:01:26.761 --> 00:01:33.963
"We'll never get there by five o'clock—it's half past four now," said Diana with a despairing look at

20
00:01:34.003 --> 00:01:34.463
her watch.

21
00:01:34.483 --> 00:01:36.124
"Let's keep going.

22
00:01:36.544 --> 00:01:37.944
I think there's a short cut ahead."

23
00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:41.305
A few minutes later, the road forked again.

24
00:01:41.325 --> 00:01:44.366
"Which road do we take?"

25
00:01:44.846 --> 00:01:46.167
asked Diana anxiously.

26
00:01:47.347 --> 00:01:48.207
Anne shook her head.

27
00:01:48.227 --> 00:01:50.088
"I don't know.

28
00:01:51.052 --> 00:01:53.894
There's a gate and a lane leading right into the woods.

29
00:01:54.795 --> 00:01:56.316
There must be a house at the end.

30
00:01:56.957 --> 00:01:58.278
Let's go there and inquire."

31
00:01:58.298 --> 00:02:03.502
"What a romantic old lane this is," said Diana.

32
00:02:03.522 --> 00:02:07.985
"It's like an enchanted forest," said Anne.

33
00:02:09.666 --> 00:02:13.149
Diana exclaimed, "Oh, I know where we are now.

34
00:02:13.649 --> 00:02:16.732
That is the little stone house where Miss Lavender Lewis lives."

35
00:02:18.316 --> 00:02:23.958
"It's the sweetest, prettiest place I ever saw or imagined," said Anne with delight.

36
00:02:23.978 --> 00:02:28.279
"It looks like something from a storybook."

37
00:02:29.179 --> 00:02:32.140
The house was built of stone and was covered in ivy.

38
00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:38.342
"It will be interesting to meet Miss Lewis said Diana as they opened the gate into the garden.

39
00:02:38.362 --> 00:02:41.723
"I've heard she is very peculiar."

40
00:02:41.743 --> 00:02:45.504
"She'll be interesting then," said Anne firmly.

41
00:02:46.264 --> 00:02:49.126
"Peculiar people are always interesting at least!"

42
00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:51.967
They reached the front door and knocked.

43
00:02:53.508 --> 00:02:57.890
"She used to be engaged to Stephen Irving, Paul's father," Diana said.

44
00:02:57.910 --> 00:03:00.712
"But they quarreled and parted."

45
00:03:00.732 --> 00:03:03.133
"Hush," warned Anne.

46
00:03:03.153 --> 00:03:05.014
"The door is opening."

47
00:03:06.515 --> 00:03:10.377
A girl of about 14 opened the door and showed them into the parlor.

48
00:03:10.397 --> 00:03:15.700
"Miss Lavender must be expecting company for tea," Anne whispered.

49
00:03:16.312 --> 00:03:18.474
"There are six places set at the table."

50
00:03:20.396 --> 00:03:22.157
Miss Lavender Lewis came in.

51
00:03:23.158 --> 00:03:26.481
She was a little lady with light hair and big brown eyes.

52
00:03:26.501 --> 00:03:31.145
"We wanted to ask the right way to Grafton," said Diana.

53
00:03:31.165 --> 00:03:33.907
"We took the wrong path coming through the woods.

54
00:03:34.908 --> 00:03:36.589
Do we go left or right at your gate?"

55
00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.632
"Left," said Miss Lavender.

56
00:03:40.793 --> 00:03:44.376
Then she exclaimed, "But, oh, won't you stay and have tea with me?

57
00:03:45.568 --> 00:03:46.248
Please do!

58
00:03:46.908 --> 00:03:51.130
You'll get to Grafton too late, and Charlotte and I would love for you to stay."

59
00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:57.952
"We'd like to stay," said Anne promptly, for she wanted to get to know Miss Lavender better.

60
00:03:57.972 --> 00:04:01.593
"But you are expecting other guests, aren't you?"

61
00:04:01.613 --> 00:04:06.054
"I know you'll think I'm silly," she said.

62
00:04:06.074 --> 00:04:07.455
"I am silly.

63
00:04:07.475 --> 00:04:09.435
I'm not expecting anybody.

64
00:04:09.455 --> 00:04:11.136
I was just pretending.

65
00:04:11.948 --> 00:04:16.969
You see, I was so lonely and I love company, but few people ever come here because it

66
00:04:17.029 --> 00:04:18.550
is so far out of the way.

67
00:04:19.390 --> 00:04:20.770
Charlotte was lonely too.

68
00:04:21.931 --> 00:04:26.492
So I baked a cake and got dressed up, but we were just pretending."

69
00:04:28.993 --> 00:04:33.034
Diana secretly thought Miss Lavender was just as peculiar as she had heard.

70
00:04:34.434 --> 00:04:38.555
A woman of 45 pretending to have a tea party, as if she was a little girl!

71
00:04:39.515 --> 00:04:44.706
But Anne exclaimed joyfully, "Oh, do you imagine things too?"

72
00:04:46.026 --> 00:04:49.149
"Yes, I do," Miss Lavender confessed boldly.

73
00:04:49.169 --> 00:04:54.172
"Of course it's silly, but being silly doesn't hurt anybody, and it's fun!

74
00:04:54.192 --> 00:04:57.595
Now, let's sit down and eat everything!"

75
00:04:57.975 --> 00:04:58.675
she went on.

76
00:04:59.296 --> 00:05:01.818
And then they all had a lovely afternoon tea.

77
00:05:02.298 --> 00:05:05.840
As it grew dark, it became time for Anne and Diana to leave.

78
00:05:05.860 --> 00:05:07.862
"You will come again?"

79
00:05:08.262 --> 00:05:09.363
Miss Lavender asked.

80
00:05:09.383 --> 00:05:10.724
"Of course!"

81
00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:12.762
Anne exclaimed and smiled.

82
00:05:13.622 --> 00:05:16.505
She had decided Miss Lavender was a kindred spirit.

83
00:05:17.746 --> 00:05:20.748
As Anne and Diana left, they thanked Miss Lavender.

84
00:05:20.768 --> 00:05:23.811
"Paul Irving would love it here!"

85
00:05:24.231 --> 00:05:25.853
Anne said quietly to herself.

86
00:05:25.873 --> 00:05:28.315
"Paul Irving?"

87
00:05:28.715 --> 00:05:29.776
Miss Lavender asked.

88
00:05:30.337 --> 00:05:34.240
There was a subtle change in her face, and her voice sounded a little different.

89
00:05:35.201 --> 00:05:35.801
"Who is he?

90
00:05:35.821 --> 00:05:38.504
I don't know anybody of that name in Avonlea."

91
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.701
Anne was annoyed that she had accidentally mentioned Paul Irving's name.

92
00:05:44.782 --> 00:05:48.543
She had forgotten about Miss Lavender's old romance with Paul's father.

93
00:05:48.563 --> 00:05:51.984
"He is a student of mine," said Anne.

94
00:05:52.004 --> 00:05:56.365
"He moved from Boston to Avonlea this year to live with his grandmother."

95
00:05:56.385 --> 00:05:59.306
"Is he Stephen Irving's son?"

96
00:05:59.686 --> 00:06:00.786
Miss Lavender asked.

97
00:06:02.007 --> 00:06:04.207
"Yes, he is," Anne answered.

98
00:06:05.568 --> 00:06:11.196
"Here's some lavender," said Miss Lavender brightly, as if she had not heard the answer to her question.

99
00:06:11.216 --> 00:06:16.120
"Father named me Lavender because he was so fond of it."

100
00:06:17.621 --> 00:06:19.763
Anne and Diana waved good-bye and left.

101
00:06:21.805 --> 00:06:24.367
Diana said, "She seems a little lonely.

102
00:06:24.887 --> 00:06:26.249
We must come and visit her."

103
00:06:26.269 --> 00:06:28.811
"Yes!" Anne said.

104
00:06:28.831 --> 00:06:32.934
"Her parents named her well—sweet Miss Lavender."
